\cf0 January 5, 1937.\
Miss Margaret West\
The Hogarth Press\
52 Tavistock Square\
London, W.C.1\
Dear Miss West: \
We are enormously pleased to have your letter of December 21st with the good news that you expect to be able to send the final corrected page proof of THE YEARS about January tenth. As for the date of publication, I understand the reasons which make it essential for you to publish early, and we shall have to do the best we can to bring out our edition as soon as possible after yours. \
We decided last spring that it would be better to prepare a jacket of our own for this book, and I think I wrote to Mr. Woolf reporting that decision at the time. At any rate, I intend to inform him. \
Will you please be sure to send word of your exact publication date when it is definitely decided and to send along as soon as they are available three copies of your edition which we shall require for copyrighting and other purposes. \
Yours sincerely, \
Harcourt, Brace and Company, \
Donald Brace\
